                <pb facs="0110" n="20" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg20"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/1742: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">White</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-30T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 30,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>148. Your August 27, 7 p.m. You are instructed to refer to the Department’s
                    telegram of March 25, 6 p.m. last paragraph. If the report is confirmed that
                    Liberals intend sending Commission to Washington for the purpose stated by you,
                    you may say to the <pb facs="0111" n="21" xml:id="pg21"/> leaders of the Liberal
                    party that the Department is of the opinion that no good purpose will be served
                    by a conference in Washington with the representatives of any political party in
                    Cuba, and that the attempt to transfer the center of political activity from
                    Cuba to Washington is harmful to the best interests of Cuba and is fruitful of
                    endless misunderstandings.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
